"""Warmage subclasses, Valda's Spire of Secrets 2024 (Mage Hand Press). Own wording."""
SUB = {
"House of Bishops": {"spab": "INT",
 "f": {
  "Arcane Study": "You gain proficiency in two skills of your choice from Arcana, History, Investigation, Medicine, and Religion.",
  "Spellcasting": "You can cast more powerful spells. **Spell Slots.** The Bishop Spellcasting table gives your slots for level 1+ spells. A Long Rest restores all of them. **Prepared Spells of Level 1+.** You keep a list of prepared level 1+ spells. Start with three level 1 Wizard spells. Burning Hands, Grease, and Shield are good picks. The list grows as the Prepared Spells column shows. When it grows, add Wizard spells until the list matches the table. Each spell must be a level you have slots for. Example: at Warmage level 7 your list can hold five Wizard spells of levels 1 and 2 in any mix. **Changing Your Prepared Spells.** When you gain a Warmage level, you can swap one spell on the list for another Wizard spell you have slots for. **Warmage Edge.** You can use Warmage Edge on damage rolls of level 1+ Wizard spells as if they were cantrips. With Magic Missile, it improves the roll of only one dart.",
  "Mystical Companion": "Find Familiar is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells. When you cast it, your familiar can take a normal form or one of these: Imp, Pseudodragon, Quasit, or Sprite.",
  "Siege Casting": "Your Warmage and Wizard spells deal double damage to objects and structures. You have Advantage on spell attack rolls against targets 100 feet or more away.",
  "Spell Sculpting": "When you cast a spell with a spell slot that affects other creatures you can see, choose up to a number of them equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one). Those creatures automatically succeed on their saves against it and take no damage if they would take half on a success.",
  "Arcane Dominance": "As a Bonus Action, you can expend spell slots with a combined level of 6 or more to regain one expended use of Arcane Surge."},
 "acts": {"Arcane Dominance": "bonus"}},

"House of Cards": {"spab": "",
 "f": {
  "Bluff": "You gain proficiency in Deception and with the Gaming Kit (Playing Cards) if you lack it. You also add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to Charisma (Deception) checks.",
  "Deck of Fate": "You have a magical deck of playing or tarot cards that boosts your cantrips. Shuffle a standard 52-card deck and draw five cards when you roll Initiative. Whenever you target an enemy with a Warmage spell that deals damage, you can use a Bonus Action to play one or more cards from your hand. If the cards exactly match a result on the Hands table, the spell deals extra damage to one target of your choice or gives you the listed effect. Otherwise nothing happens. Aces count as ones. Played cards go to the bottom of the deck, then you draw back up to five. **Hands.** Straight (five sequential cards of any suit): extra 12 damage. Flush (five cards of one suit): extra 10 damage. Three of a Kind: extra 6 damage. Pair: extra 2 damage. Hearts (any two): Temporary Hit Points equal to your Intelligence modifier. Spades (any two): Speed +10 feet until the start of your next turn. Diamonds (any two): +1 AC until the start of your next turn. Clubs (any two): +1 to saving throws until the start of your next turn.",
  "High Stakes": "On your turn, you can put any number of cards from your hand on the bottom of your deck (no action needed), losing 2 Hit Points per card. Then draw back up to five cards.",
  "Dealer's Choice": "As a Bonus Action, you gain one of these benefits, chosen by the GM. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest. **Resistance.** Resistance to all damage until the end of your next turn. **Teleportation.** You teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 60 feet. **Demiplane.** You vanish into a safe, endless demiplane. At the start of your next turn you return to your space, or the nearest free space if it is taken.",
  "Card Reading": "Once on each of your turns, when you draw a card for Deck of Fate, you can name a suit (Clubs, Diamonds, Hearts, or Spades) and look at the top card of your deck. If you named the suit correctly, you can take the Dash, Disengage, or Utilize action as part of the Bonus Action used for Deck of Fate.",
  "Ace in the Hole": "When you would draw cards from your deck, draw twice as many. Put half of them on the bottom of the deck and the rest in your hand."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Dealer's Choice", "n": "Dealer's Choice", "lvl": 10, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Bonus Action"}],
 "acts": {"Deck of Fate": "bonus", "Dealer's Choice": "bonus"},
 "fx": [[3, "Bluff", {"skills": ["Deception"]}]],
 "grant": {"f": "Bluff", "tools": [[3, "Playing Cards"]]}},

"House of Darts": {"spab": "",
 "f": {
  "Bullseye": "Record the d20 number whenever you make a ranged spell attack roll with a Warmage cantrip. With Advantage or Disadvantage, record the higher or lower die. If Trick Shot changes the d20, record the new number. A recorded number lasts 1 minute. When you roll a recorded number on a spell attack roll with a Warmage cantrip, pick one benefit. **Extra Damage.** The target takes an extra 1d10 Force damage. **Recovery.** You regain one expended use of Trick Shot. **Reroll.** Reroll the d20 and use the new roll, and record it.",
  "Magic Daggers": "You learn the Magic Daggers cantrip.",
  "Trick Shot": "You bend your shots mid-air. When you make a ranged attack roll with a Warmage cantrip or a Thrown weapon, you can add or subtract a d4 from the d20, to a maximum of 20 and a minimum of 1. Raising the roll to 20 this way is not a Critical Hit. You can use this after seeing the roll, which may turn a miss into a hit. You can use it a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once). A Short Rest returns one expended use. A Long Rest returns all of them.",
  "Dagger Climb": "You can cast Magic Daggers to summon a pair of daggers into your open hands to help you climb. You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed for 10 minutes.",
  "Intercepting Shot": "As a Reaction when an attacker you can see within 60 feet attacks you or an Ally you can see within 30 feet of you, you can make a ranged spell attack with Magic Daggers to interrupt it. If your roll beats the attacker's roll, you can reduce the attack roll against you by 5, to a minimum result of 1.",
  "Vanishing Toss": "When you cast Magic Daggers, you can replace one of its spell attacks by throwing a special teleportation dagger to a point you can see within range. While you are within 500 feet of it, you can use a Bonus Action to teleport to the dagger. It disappears after 10 minutes, or when you teleport with it or throw another one.",
  "Dart Burst": "If you have recorded ten or more different numbers with Bullseye, you can use a Magic action to clear all recorded numbers and throw a burst of darts. Each creature in a 60-foot Cone makes a Dexterity save. A creature takes 1d8 Force damage per different recorded number on a failure, or half as much on a success. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Long Rest."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Trick Shot", "n": "Trick Shot", "lvl": 3, "max": "mod:INT", "reset": "long", "tag": "Short Rest 1"},
        {"feature": "Dart Burst", "n": "Dart Burst", "lvl": 18, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "Magic action"}],
 "acts": {"Intercepting Shot": "reaction", "Vanishing Toss": "bonus", "Dart Burst": "action"}},

"House of Dice": {"spab": "",
 "f": {
  "Bonus Proficiencies": "You gain proficiency in Sleight of Hand and with the Gaming Set (Dice Set) if you lack it.",
  "Chaos Roll": "As a Magic action, you can expend two Dice of Fate and roll them on the Chaos Roll table. **2.** You cast Fireball centered on yourself. **3.** Your AC drops by 2 until the start of your next turn. **4.** You have the Prone condition. **5.** Until the start of your next turn, each creature in a 60-foot Emanation from you can speak only babbling nonsense and cannot cast spells with a Verbal component. **6.** A 5-foot-radius Sphere of butterflies, insects, or doves fills a spot you choose within 60 feet. It is Heavily Obscured until the start of your next turn. **7.** You gain 7 Temporary Hit Points and keep the Dice of Fate instead of giving them to the GM. **8.** You have the Invisible condition until the end of your next turn, as per Invisibility. **9.** A small explosion hits an enemy chosen by the GM for 3d6 Fire damage. **10.** You teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Each creature within 5 feet of the destination makes a Dexterity save against your spell save DC or takes 2d6 Force damage. **11.** Choose a creature you can see within 60 feet. It takes 4d6 Necrotic damage and you regain Hit Points equal to the damage dealt. **12.** You cast Lightning Bolt and can add the Dice of Fate to its damage roll.",
  "Dice of Fate": "You have four Dice of Fate, which are d6s. When you fail a D20 Test or make a damage roll, you can expend a Die of Fate and add it to the roll, which may turn a failed D20 Test into a success. An expended die goes to the GM, who can spend it on a D20 Test or damage roll for an NPC or monster. When the GM spends it, it comes back to you, and so on. A Long Rest restores all your expended Dice of Fate, whether or not the GM used them. From Warmage level 7, you have two more dice (six), and you can add two Dice of Fate at once to damage rolls of Warmage cantrips.",
  "Loaded Dice": "Once on each of your turns when you roll a d6, you can flip the die upside down. On a d6, the top and bottom faces add to 7.",
  "Twisted Fate": "When you make an attack roll or ability check with Disadvantage on your turn, you can use a Bonus Action to try to invert fate. Expend a Die of Fate and roll it. On a 5, you ignore the Disadvantage. On a 6, you have Advantage on the roll instead.",
  "Roll the Bones": "As a Reaction when a creature you can see damages you, you can expend two Dice of Fate to make a Chaos Roll.",
  "Steal Luck": "When you roll Initiative, roll a d6. You take back that many Dice of Fate from the GM."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Dice of Fate", "n": "Dice of Fate", "lvl": 3, "max": [0, 0, 4, 4, 4, 4, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6], "reset": "long", "tag": "d6"}],
 "acts": {"Chaos Roll": "action", "Twisted Fate": "bonus", "Roll the Bones": "reaction"},
 "fx": [[3, "Bonus Proficiencies", {"skills": ["Sleight of Hand"]}]],
 "grant": {"f": "Bonus Proficiencies", "tools": [[3, "Dice Set"]]}},

"House of Go": {"spab": "",
 "f": {
  "Formations": "You learn tactics called Formations. As a Bonus Action you can activate one. It lasts until you and your Ally are no longer in it, you are Incapacitated, you die, or you activate a different one. **Flank.** Use it when you and an Ally without the Incapacitated condition are adjacent to an enemy on opposite sides. A 5-foot-wide Line from your space through the centers of all three spaces shows this. You and your Ally have Advantage on attack rolls against the flanked creature. **Solo.** Use it when no Ally is within 5 feet of you. If you target a creature with a cantrip, it cannot make Opportunity Attacks against you for the rest of the turn or until you leave the formation, whether or not the cantrip deals damage. **Wall.** Use it when you and two to six Allies without the Incapacitated condition are each within 5 feet of another Ally. Each creature in the formation, you included, gains +2 AC.",
  "Opening Strategy": "You can spend 10 minutes planning an encounter in detail. Share the plan with up to six Allies within 30 feet who can see or hear and understand you. Each Ally who understands it can gain Advantage on one attack roll or ability check in the next 10 minutes. An Ally who rolls Initiative in that time cannot use this to gain Advantage after the first round of combat ends. Once you make a plan, you cannot do so again until you finish a Long Rest.",
  "Hardened Formations": "While you are in a formation, any Critical Hit against you or an Ally in your formation becomes a normal hit.",
  "Chain of Liberties": "Your formation moves as if your Allies were chain links. When you move on your turn, any number of willing Allies in your formation can move the same distance.",
  "End Game": "On your turn, when you reduce a creature to 0 Hit Points with a Warmage cantrip, you can cast another cantrip as a Bonus Action. You can apply Warmage Edge to it even if you already used Warmage Edge this turn."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Opening Strategy", "n": "Opening Strategy", "lvl": 7, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "10 minutes"}],
 "acts": {"Formations": "bonus"}},

"House of Kings": {"spab": "",
 "f": {
  "Battle Tactics": "You learn maneuvers powered by special Battle Dice. **Battle Dice.** You have two Battle Dice, which are d6s. A die is expended when you use it. You regain all expended Battle Dice when you roll Initiative or finish a Short or Long Rest. The die type and number grow as the Battle Dice table shows: 2d6 at level 3, 3d6 at level 7, 3d8 at level 13, 4d8 at level 19. **Maneuvers.** You spend Battle Dice to perform maneuvers. **Saving Throws.** A maneuver's save DC equals your spell save DC.",
  "Maneuver Options": "Your maneuver options are Blitz, Check, Flash of Brilliance, Gambit, Morale Boost, and Stalemate. **Blitz.** When you hit a creature with an attack, spend a Battle Die as a Bonus Action to add it to the damage roll. An Ally within 60 feet who can see or hear you can use a Reaction to move up to its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks. **Check.** When you hit a creature with an attack, spend a Battle Die as a Bonus Action to add it to the damage roll. The target has the Frightened condition until the end of your next turn. **Flash of Brilliance.** When you fail an Intelligence or Wisdom check, spend a Battle Die and add it to the roll, which may turn it into a success. Once per turn. **Gambit.** When you hit a creature with an attack, spend a Battle Die as a Bonus Action to add it to the damage roll. The next creature other than you to make an attack roll against the target adds the die to that roll. **Morale Boost.** When an ally you can see within 60 feet fails a saving throw, use a Reaction to spend a Battle Die and add it to the roll, which may turn it into a success. **Stalemate.** When you hit a creature with an attack, spend a Battle Die as a Bonus Action to add it to the damage roll. The target must succeed on a Strength save or its Speed becomes 0 until the end of its next turn.",
  "Martial Training": "You gain proficiency with Martial weapons and training with Medium armor and Shields.",
  "Lead from the Front": "Difficult Terrain costs you no extra movement. Allies within 120 feet who can see you gain this benefit too.",
  "Tactical Master": "Allies within 10 feet of you add your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) to saving throws against spells and magical effects.",
  "Checkmate [Maneuver]": "When you hit a creature with an attack, you can spend a Battle Die as a Bonus Action to direct an Ally within 60 feet who can see or hear you to strike. The Ally can use a Reaction to cast a cantrip or make one weapon attack or Unarmed Strike. The Ally adds the Battle Die to one damage roll of that attack or cantrip.",
  "Grandmaster": "When you roll Initiative, choose up to a number of Allies equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum one) within 60 feet who can see or hear you. Give each a Battle Die without expending it. Once in the next minute, when that Ally fails a D20 Test, it can roll the die and add the result to the d20, which may turn the failure into a success. The die is expended when rolled."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Battle Tactics", "n": "Battle Dice", "lvl": 3, "max": [0, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4], "reset": "short", "tag": "d6, d8 from level 13"}],
 "acts": {"Checkmate [Maneuver]": "bonus"},
 "fx": [[3, "Martial Training", {"notes": [["Note", "Martial Training: Martial weapons, Medium armor, and Shield training"]]}]]},

"House of Knights": {"spab": "",
 "f": {
  "Martial Training": "You gain proficiency with Martial weapons and training with Medium armor, Heavy armor, and Shields. You can ignore the Strength requirement for Heavy armor and for weapons with the Heavy property.",
  "Mystical Armament": "You blend swordplay and arcana. **Martial Cantrips.** You learn the Force Buckler cantrip and one of these: Arc Blade, Burning Blade, Frigid Blade, or True Strike. **Manifest Weapon.** As a Bonus Action, you can create a Simple or Martial Melee weapon of magical force in your hand. It counts as worth 1 GP for Material components and works as a Spellcasting Focus. You can use your Intelligence modifier instead of Strength or Dexterity for its attack and damage rolls. It deals Force damage or its normal damage type. It vanishes at the end of your turn if you are not holding it.",
  "Fighting Style": "You gain a Fighting Style feat of your choice. When you gain a Warmage level, you can swap it for a different Fighting Style feat.",
  "Knight's Ward": "As a Bonus Action, you raise a hardened magical barrier and gain Temporary Hit Points equal to twice your Warmage level. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.",
  "Tactical Maneuver": "You can spend up to 30 feet of movement to teleport to an unoccupied space you can see. The destination can be as many feet away as half the movement you spend.",
  "Field of Blades": "As a Magic action, you summon a whirlwind of mystical weapons and make a melee spell attack against up to five creatures you can see within 30 feet, with a separate roll for each. On a hit, a target takes Force damage equal to 2d10 plus your Intelligence modifier."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Knight's Ward", "n": "Knight's Ward", "lvl": 10, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Bonus Action"}],
 "acts": {"Mystical Armament": "bonus", "Knight's Ward": "bonus", "Field of Blades": "action"},
 "fx": [[3, "Martial Training", {"notes": [["Note", "Martial Training: Martial weapons, Medium and Heavy armor, and Shield training. Ignore Strength requirements for Heavy armor and Heavy weapons"]]}]]},

"House of Pawns": {"spab": "",
 "f": {
  "Promotion": "You train as the model Warmage. When you finish a Long Rest, choose one benefit. It lasts until you choose a different one with this feature. **Adaptive Magic.** You learn one Warmage trick you qualify for and one Warmage cantrip of your choice. The trick does not count against your tricks known. **Martial Training.** You gain proficiency with Martial weapons and training with Medium armor and Shields.",
  "Pawn Storm": "You add your Intelligence modifier (minimum 1) to Initiative rolls. When you roll Initiative, you can also move up to your Speed.",
  "Multidiscipline": "You add half your Proficiency Bonus, rounded down, to any saving throw that does not already use your Proficiency Bonus.",
  "Pawn Wall": "When a Warmage cantrip deals damage, you and up to two Allies within 5 feet of you have Resistance to that damage type until the end of your next turn.",
  "Fundamental Mastery": "Once per turn when you roll damage for a Warmage cantrip, you can pick one damage die and treat it as having rolled its maximum."}},

"House of Rooks": {"spab": "",
 "f": {
  "Arcane Acrobat": "You gain proficiency in one skill of your choice from Acrobatics, Sleight of Hand, and Stealth. You also add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to all your Dexterity checks.",
  "Rook Strike": "When you make an attack roll or ability check, you can use a Bonus Action to gain Advantage on it. Or you can impose Disadvantage on a creature's saving throw against a Warmage cantrip you cast before the end of your turn. You can use this a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once). A Short Rest returns one expended use. A Long Rest returns all of them.",
  "Covert Magic": "You can cast Feather Fall, Invisibility, Knock, Silence, and Spider Climb each once without a spell slot or Verbal components. Knock is silent when cast this way. After you cast a spell with this feature, you cannot cast it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can expend a use of Arcane Surge to regain your use of all these spells (no action needed).",
  "Fleeting Decoy": "When a creature you can see damages you, you can use a Reaction to raise a defensive illusion. Attacks against you have Disadvantage until the start of your next turn.",
  "Elusive Step": "If you move more than 5 feet on your turn, your further movement that turn does not provoke Opportunity Attacks.",
  "Arcane Assassin": "You can cast Greater Invisibility on yourself only, without a spell slot or spell components. While you have the Invisible condition, your Speed is doubled. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Rook Strike", "n": "Rook Strike", "lvl": 3, "max": "mod:INT", "reset": "long", "tag": "Bonus Action, Short Rest 1"},
        {"feature": "Covert Magic", "n": "Covert Magic", "lvl": 7, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "Each of 5 spells once"},
        {"feature": "Arcane Assassin", "n": "Arcane Assassin", "lvl": 18, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Greater Invisibility"}],
 "acts": {"Rook Strike": "bonus", "Fleeting Decoy": "reaction"}},

"House of Roulette": {"spab": "",
 "f": {
  "Spin the Wheel": "You have an arcane roulette ball and chips. As a Bonus Action, you conjure a wheel of magical force and roll the ball. Choose bets from the Roulette Bets table, announce your guess, and roll a d100. You gain the listed benefit for each correct guess. **Chips of Fate.** You have four Chips of Fate and regain all expended chips when you finish a Long Rest. You gain two more at level 7 (6), level 10 (8), and level 15 (10). When you bet, you can spend 1 to 4 chips to place that many extra bets. You can place only two types of bet per d100 roll, such as Singles and Tens, and only one Odd/Even and one High/Low bet. If you win two bets on the same roll, you gain both benefits. **Roulette Bets.** Odd/Even (guess odd or even): +2 AC until the start of your next turn. High/Low (guess above or below 50): +2 to attack rolls until the start of your next turn. Lanes (guess which span holds the number: 01-20, 21-40, 41-60, 61-80, or 81-00): Advantage on a D20 Test before the end of your next turn. Tens (guess the tens digit): once before the end of your next turn, add 10 to the damage roll of a Warmage cantrip. Single (guess the exact number): until the start of your next turn you have Resistance to all damage and treat any d20 roll you make as a 20.",
  "Lucky Number": "Pick a Lucky Number from 1 to 100. If that number comes up on any d100 roll from Spin the Wheel, you gain the benefit of betting it as a Single. You can change your Lucky Number when you finish a Long Rest.",
  "Spinning Shield": "When a creature you can see makes an attack roll against you, you can use a Reaction to conjure the wheel between you and the attacker. You and the attacker each roll a d100. If your roll is equal or higher, the attack misses. You cannot use this again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.",
  "Cash Out": "As a Bonus Action, you can expend a Chip of Fate to teleport up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.",
  "Everything on Black": "When you roll Initiative, you regain 4 expended Chips of Fate. When you spend chips to bet on a Single and win, you regain all your expended Chips of Fate."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Spin the Wheel", "n": "Chips of Fate", "lvl": 3, "max": [0, 0, 4, 4, 4, 4, 6, 6, 6, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10], "reset": "long", "tag": "Bonus Action"},
        {"feature": "Spinning Shield", "n": "Spinning Shield", "lvl": 10, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Reaction"}],
 "acts": {"Spin the Wheel": "bonus", "Spinning Shield": "reaction", "Cash Out": "bonus"}},
}
